%% assets/ files absent from the output. And the change landed on PRECISELY this
%% diagram's declared subject: a gate, and what it could not see.
%% -
%% THE FIX, which is a THIRD failure mode in the same family as the other two.
%%   resolve_mmdc() called shutil.which("mmdc") for its TRUTHINESS and then
%%   passed the bare string "mmdc" to subprocess. On Windows mermaid-cli
%%   installs as mmdc.cmd; `which` finds it because it consults PATHEXT, and
%%   `subprocess` without a shell does not, because CreateProcess searches for
%%   the literal name and name+.exe only. So on a machine where mermaid-cli WAS
%%   installed, the call raised an uncaught WinError 2 -- and MMDC_MISSING, the
%%   message written for exactly that moment, never printed, because `which` had
%%   already succeeded. The resolved path is now the return value :219-224, for
%%   the npx branch as well; both branches had it and both are fixed.
%%   Fixed in 1.2.4, and SKILL.md gained the same explanation in prose (its only
%%   hunk in this range) so whichever one a reader hits first is enough.
%% -
%%   SECOND HALF OF THE SAME FIX, and it is the part that keeps the message:
%%   subprocess.run is now wrapped :241-252, and an OSError -- a shim pointing
%%   at a deleted install, a wrong-architecture binary, a lost execute bit --
%%   sys.exits with MMDC_MISSING plus the resolved path, rather than escaping as
%%   a traceback that loses it. sys.exit and not RuntimeError on purpose: an
%%   unusable launcher is unusable for every diagram, so retrying the rest only
%%   buries the message.
%% -
%%   Why this belongs on THIS diagram rather than in a footnote: every other
